5. Core Narrative

The central engineering idea is:

AI coding agents are capable workers, but autonomous software delivery requires engineering management around the agent.

The case study should explain the shift from:

Human
  ↓
Prompt AI
  ↓
Review Code
  ↓
Run Build
  ↓
Explain Failure
  ↓
Prompt AI Again
  ↓
Choose Next Task
  ↓
Repeat

to:

Human Defines Product Intent
          ↓
Documentation Defines Engineering Intent
          ↓
Deterministic Task Backlog
          ↓
Execution Guardrails
          ↓
AI Coding Agent Executes One Task
          ↓
Validation
          ↓
Repair
          ↓
Commit
          ↓
Next Executable Task

The important lesson is not:

AI built an entire application from one prompt.

Do not use that framing.

The intended lesson is:

A structured engineering execution system allowed an AI coding agent to work through a documented backlog with reduced continuous human task management.

⸻

6. Explain the Origin of ADO

Explain the original problem.

AI coding agents can:

* generate code
* generate tests
* inspect repositories
* repair many implementation failures

But developers still frequently manage:

* next-task selection
* context assembly
* documentation retrieval
* build execution
* failure interpretation
* repair prompting
* quality validation
* progress tracking
* Git workflow

Explain that this observation led to the ADO concept:

AI agents are workers. ADO is the engineering manager.

Do not claim ADO replaces engineering managers.

Explain this as a software orchestration metaphor and product design principle.

